# Opening and closing folds. Nested cases start on line 3 with an inner fold on lines
# 3-4 inside an outer fold on lines 2-5, both closed.

=== zo opens the fold under the cursor
ref:    fold.txt *zo*
quote:  Open one fold under the cursor.
given:
  one
  |two
  three
  four
keys:   zfjzoj
expect:
  one
  two
  |three
  four

=== zc closes the fold under the cursor
ref:    fold.txt *zc*
quote:  Close one fold under the cursor.
given:
  one
  |two
  three
  four
keys:   zfjzozcj
expect:
  one
  two
  three
  |four

=== zc sets foldenable
ref:    fold.txt *zc*
quote:  'foldenable' will be set.
given:
  one
  |two
  three
  four
keys:   zfjznzcj
expect:
  one
  two
  three
  |four

=== za opens a closed fold
ref:    fold.txt *za*
quote:  When on a closed fold: open it.
given:
  one
  |two
  three
  four
keys:   zfjzaj
expect:
  one
  two
  |three
  four

=== za closes an open fold
ref:    fold.txt *za*
quote:  When on an open fold: close it and set 'foldenable'.
given:
  one
  |two
  three
  four
keys:   zfjzazaj
expect:
  one
  two
  three
  |four

=== zo opens one level of nested folds
ref:    fold.txt *zo*
quote:  Open one fold under the cursor.
given:
  one
  two
  |three
  four
  five
  six
keys:   :3,4fold<CR>:2,5fold<CR>zoj
expect:
  one
  two
  three
  four
  |five
  six

=== 2zo opens two levels
ref:    fold.txt *zo*
quote:  When a count is given, that many folds deep will be opened.
given:
  one
  two
  |three
  four
  five
  six
keys:   :3,4fold<CR>:2,5fold<CR>2zoj
expect:
  one
  two
  three
  |four
  five
  six

=== zO opens nested folds recursively
ref:    fold.txt *zO*
quote:  Open all folds under the cursor recursively.
given:
  one
  two
  |three
  four
  five
  six
keys:   :3,4fold<CR>:2,5fold<CR>zOj
expect:
  one
  two
  three
  |four
  five
  six

=== zO opens folds nested in the fold under the cursor
ref:    fold.txt *zO*
quote:  Open all folds under the cursor recursively.
given:
  one
  |two
  three
  four
  five
  six
keys:   :3,4fold<CR>:2,5fold<CR>zOjj
expect:
  one
  two
  three
  |four
  five
  six

=== zO leaves folds without the cursor line alone
ref:    fold.txt *zO*
quote:  Folds that don't contain the cursor line are unchanged.
given:
  one
  |two
  three
  four
  five
  six
  seven
  eight
keys:   :5,6fold<CR>:2,3fold<CR>zOjjjj
expect:
  one
  two
  three
  four
  five
  six
  |seven
  eight

=== zc closes the innermost open fold
ref:    fold.txt *zc*
quote:  Close one fold under the cursor.
given:
  one
  two
  |three
  four
  five
  six
keys:   :3,4fold<CR>:2,5fold<CR>zOzcj
expect:
