=== zA opens a closed fold recursively
ref:    fold.txt *zA*
quote:  When on a closed fold: open it recursively.
given:
  one
  two
  |three
  four
  five
  six
keys:   :3,4fold<CR>:2,5fold<CR>zAj
expect:
  one
  two
  three
  |four
  five
  six

=== zA closes an open fold recursively
ref:    fold.txt *zA*
quote:  When on an open fold: close it recursively and set 'foldenable'.
given:
  one
  two
  |three
  four
  five
  six
keys:   :3,4fold<CR>:2,5fold<CR>zOzAj
expect:
  one
  two
  three
  four
  five
  |six

=== zv opens just enough folds to show the cursor line
ref:    fold.txt *zv*
quote:  View cursor line: Open just enough folds to make the line in which the cursor is located not folded.
given:
  one
  two
  |three
  four
  five
  six
keys:   :3,4fold<CR>:2,5fold<CR>zvj
expect:
  one
  two
  three
  |four
  five
  six

=== zx re-applies foldlevel and then shows the cursor line
ref:    fold.txt *zx*
quote:  Undo manually opened and closed folds: re-apply 'foldlevel', then do "zv": View cursor line.
given:
  one
  two
  |three
  four
  five
  six
keys:   :3,4fold<CR>:2,5fold<CR>zOjzxj
expect:
  one
  two
  three
  four
  |five
  six

=== zx closes manually opened folds away from the cursor
ref:    fold.txt *zx*
quote:  Undo manually opened and closed folds: re-apply 'foldlevel'
given:
  one
  two
  |three
  four
  five
  six
keys:   :3,4fold<CR>:2,5fold<CR>zOggzxjj
expect:
  one
  two
  three
  four
  five
  |six

=== zX re-applies foldlevel without opening the cursor line
ref:    fold.txt *zX*
quote:  Undo manually opened and closed folds: re-apply 'foldlevel'.
given:
  one
  two
  |three
  four
  five
  six
keys:   :3,4fold<CR>:2,5fold<CR>zOjzXj
expect:
  one
  two
  three
  four
  five
  |six

=== zR opens all folds
ref:    fold.txt *zR*
quote:  Open all folds. This sets 'foldlevel' to highest fold level.
given:
  |one
  two
  three
  four
  five
  six
keys:   :3,4fold<CR>:2,5fold<CR>zRjj
expect:
  one
  two
  |three
  four
  five
  six

=== zM closes all folds
ref:    fold.txt *zM*
quote:  Close all folds: set 'foldlevel' to 0.
given:
  |one
  two
  three
  four
  five
  six
keys:   :3,4fold<CR>:2,5fold<CR>zRzMjj
expect:
  one
  two
  three
  four
  five
  |six

=== zr opens one more level
ref:    fold.txt *zr*
quote:  Reduce folding: Add |v:count1| to 'foldlevel'.
given:
  |one
  two
  three
  four
  five
  six
keys:   :3,4fold<CR>:2,5fold<CR>zrjjj
expect:
  one
  two
  three
  four
  |five
  six

=== zm closes one more level
ref:    fold.txt *zm*
quote:  Fold more: Subtract |v:count1| from 'foldlevel'.
given:
  |one
  two
  three
  four
  five
  six
keys:   :3,4fold<CR>:2,5fold<CR>zRzmjjj
expect:
  one
  two
  three
  four
  |five
  six

=== :set foldlevel=1 closes only nested folds
ref:    fold.txt *fold-foldlevel*
quote:  When 'foldlevel' is positive, some folds are closed.
given:
  |one
  two
  three
  four
  five
  six
keys:   :3,4fold<CR>:2,5fold<CR>:set foldlevel=1<CR>jjj
expect:
  one
  two
  three
  four
  |five
  six

=== changing foldlevel re-applies it to manually opened folds
ref:    fold.txt *fold-foldlevel*
quote:  'foldlevel' is applied when it is changed.
given:
  one
  two
  |three
  four
  five
  six
keys:   :3,4fold<CR>:2,5fold<CR>zO:set fdl=1<CR>ggjjj
expect:
  one
  two
  three
  four
  |five
  six

=== zn opens every fold
ref:    fold.txt *zn*
quote:  Fold none: reset 'foldenable'. All folds will be open.
given:
  one
  |two
  three
  four
keys:   zfjznj
expect:
  one
  two
  |three
  four

=== zN restores the folds
ref:    fold.txt *zN*
quote:  Fold normal: set 'foldenable'. All folds will be as they were before.
given:
  one
  |two
  three
  four
keys:   zfjznzNj
expect:
  one
  two
  three
  |four

=== zi turns folding off
ref:    fold.txt *zi*
quote:  Invert 'foldenable'.
given:
  one
  |two
  three
  four
keys:   zfjzij
expect:
  one
  two
  |three
  four

=== zi twice turns folding back on
ref:    fold.txt *zi*
quote:  Invert 'foldenable'.
given:
  one
  |two
  three
  four
keys:   zfjzizij
expect:
  one
  two
  three
  |four

=== :foldopen opens one level in the range
ref:    fold.txt *:foldopen*
quote:  Without [!] one level of folds is opened.
given:
  one
  two
  |three
  four
  five
  six
keys:   :3,4fold<CR>:2,5fold<CR>:2,5foldopen<CR>j
expect:
  one
  two
  three
  four
  |five
  six

=== :foldopen! opens every fold in the range
ref:    fold.txt *:foldopen*
quote:  When [!] is added all folds are opened.
given:
  one
  two
  |three
  four
  five
  six
keys:   :3,4fold<CR>:2,5fold<CR>:2,5foldopen!<CR>j
expect:
  one
  two
  three
  |four
  five
  six

=== :foldclose closes one level in the range
ref:    fold.txt *:foldclose*
quote:  Without [!] one level of folds is closed.
given:
  one
  two
  |three
  four
  five
  six
keys:   :3,4fold<CR>:2,5fold<CR>zR:3foldclose<CR>j
expect:
  one
  two
  three
  four
  |five
  six

=== :foldclose! closes every fold in the range
ref:    fold.txt *:foldclose*
quote:  When [!] is added all folds are closed.
given:
  one
  two
  |three
  four
  five
  six
keys:   :3,4fold<CR>:2,5fold<CR>zR:3foldclose!<CR>j
expect:
